9443`) via `th2-revproxyp-fe1` (`172.30.198.33:9443`) and Centreon Central Web (`th2-centprop-be1` — `172.30.198.49:443`), so the **\"Test connection to server\"** button for `MAP Engine server address` succeeds.\n* **Core Discovery**: The \"Test connection to server\" button for `MAP Engine server address` is **NOT executed by PHP on the Central backend**, but is executed **client-side directly in the user's web browser** via JavaScript AJAX ([`listOptions.js:266`](file:///usr/share/centreon/www/modules/centreon-map4-web-client/views/options/listOptions.js#L266)).\n\n---\n\n### 2. Progress\n* **DNS-01 Certificate Issued**:\n  * Issued official Let's Encrypt production certificate for `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr` (valid until Dec 9, 2026).\n  * Method: Executed from local Debian Trixie workstation using Certbot manual hooks with **passwordless SSH** (`id_ed25519`) to `superuser@172.30.198.162:30` (`th2-dnsp-mst1`) and `sudo pdnsutil replace-rrset` / `increase-serial`.\n  * Verified public propagation against Google DoH and Cloudflare DoH.\n* **Certifica\n<truncated 3946 bytes>\ntps;`.\n   * Verify `curl -sS https://map...:9443/centreon-map/api/latest/actuator/health` through Nginx returns `200 {\"status\":\"UP\"}`.\n2. **Workstation DNS Resolution (for Internal Testing)**:\n   * To test from an internal workstation, add `172.30.198.33 map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr` to the local workstation's `/etc/hosts` (or configure corporate split-horizon DNS) to bypass the lack of Hairpin NAT on the firewall.\n3. **Verify in Centreon Web UI**:\n   * Click **\"Test connection to server\"**; browser AJAX will receive `200 {\"status\":\"UP\"}` with matching CORS headers and turn green.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Commitments & Constraints\n* Do not restart Nginx (always `systemctl reload nginx` after `nginx -t`).\n* Never modify shared configurations without strict scoping.\n* Respect user instructions on network testing and commands.\n</summary>\n\nYou have the 2 followi