d against public resolvers (Google DoH and Cloudflare DoH) before returning to Certbot.\n19: 3. **Production Certificate Issued**:\n20:    * **Domain**: `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom\n<truncated 1801 bytes>\n **Nginx Reload**:\n45:    * `nginx -t`: **Syntax OK, test successful**.\n46:    * Reloaded without downtime.\n47: \n48: ---\n49: \n50: ## 3. End-to-End Verification Results\n51: \n52: ```mermaid\n53: flowchart LR\n54:     Central[\"th2-centprop-be1\\n(172.30.198.49)\\nCentreon Central PHP\"] -->|\"HTTPS :9443\\n(Strict TLS Verified)\"| RevProxy[\"th2-revproxyp-fe1\\n(172.30.198.33)\\nNginx Proxy\"]\n55:     ExtUser[\"External Browser\\n(map.extranetclient...)\"] -->|\"HTTPS :9443\\n(Valid Public Cert)\"| RevProxy\n56:     RevProxy -->|\"HTTPS :9443 (TLS)\\nproxy_ssl_verify off\"| Map[\"th2-centprop-map\\n(172.30.198.50)\\nTomcat Engine\"]\n57: ```\n58: \n59: | Source / Target | Test Command | Result | Status |\n60: | :--- | :--- | :--- | :---: |\n61: | **Local Machine $\\rightarrow$ Port 9443** | `openssl s_client -connect 172.30.198.33:9443` | `CN=map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr`, Issuer `Let's Encrypt (YE2)` | **VERIFIED** |\n62: | **Local Machine $\\rightarrow$ Port 9443** | `curl -sS -I https://map.extranetclient...:9443/` | `HTTP/2 301` $\\rightarrow$ `location: .../centreon-map/` (Strict TLS OK, no `-k`) | **VERIFIED** |\n63: | **Central Backend (`.49`) $\\rightarrow$ Reverse Proxy** | `curl -sS -I https://map.extranetclient...:9443/` | `HTTP/2 301` (Strict TLS OK, no `-k`, `/etc/hosts` routing OK) | **VERIFIED** |\n64: | **Central Backend (`.49`) $\\rightarrow$ Centreon Map** | `curl -sS -I https://map.extranetclient...:9443/centreon-map/` | `HTTP/2 400/401` (Centreon Map application response reached) | **VERIFIED** |\n65: \n66: ---\n67: \n68: ## 4. Final Verification in the Centreon Web UI\n69: \n70: You can now return to the Centreon Web Interface:\n71: 1. Navigate to: **`Administration > Extensions > Options`**.\n72: 2. Under the Map server settings, click **\"Test connection to server\"**.\n73: 3. Because the certificate is now natively trusted by PHP cURL with an exact SAN match for `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr`, the test will succeed with a green status.\n74: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
