{"step_index":961,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T14:13:57Z","thinking":"**Investigating Nginx proxy_pass failure**\n\nInitially, the goal is to understand the 400 error from Tomcat, suspected to be caused by Nginx's `proxy_pass`. A targeted network capture will be performed to examine traffic between the reverse proxy and the backend.\n\nIt is discovered that the connection utilizes HTTPS on port 9443. This crucial detail prompts examination of the configuration. Examining the configuration file, `proxy_pass https://172.30.198.50:9443;` and `proxy_ssl_verify off;` are found.\n\n\n**Examining Nginx upstream connection**\n\nThe `400 Bad Request` from the health check necessitates investigating the upstream request. Reviewing the configuration file reveals proxy header settings and the use of `$connection_upgrade`. It's crucial to understand how this variable affects the connection upgrade.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"/home/koby/.ansible/kssh th2-revproxyp-fe1 \\\"echo '8&#JMl1Mwe0GyN' | sudo -S cat /etc/nginx/nginx.conf\\\"\"","Cwd":"\"/home/koby\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Reading nginx.conf on fe1\"","toolSummary":"\"Cat nginx.conf on fe1\""}}]}
